human vowel scale. Roughly, I felt that—
>>>
<<<
U was a sort of oo, tending towards oh!

0 was more like the word awe than oh!

A was a very high ah, tending to the long sound of English a in fat. ^ E was very imperfect, and had the effect of a hollow low French e mixed with English u in hut.

1 was the worst vowel. It had none of the character of ai in air, but was

far from ee. The sound ' tootled '.
